  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Raytheon obligated $9.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Raytheon won 416 awards so far, with an average award size of $23.7M, and obligations are down 8.3% year over year. Obligations have varied across recent fiscal years, rising from $5.9B in FY21 to $10.8B in FY25 before falling to $9.9B in FY26. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the dominant market for Raytheon, accounting for $6.7B of FY2026 to date obligations. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounts for $1.7B, and Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing accounts for $1B. Other visible industry pockets include Engineering Services at $179M and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Propulsion Unit and Propulsion Unit Parts Manufacturing at $123M. Current-year totals are fiscal year to date and represent partial-year obligations, while the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, where award values appear, report total contract values rather than obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did Raytheon obligations change year over year?",
        "body": "Raytheon obligations fell 8.3% year over year. Raytheon obligations moved from $10.8B in FY25 to $9.9B in FY26. Historical context shows obligations grew from $5.9B in FY21 to $7.8B by FY24 before peaking at $10.8B in FY25."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where are Raytheon obligations concentrated by industry?",
        "body": "Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest industry for Raytheon at $6.7B. Raytheon also recorded $1.7B in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences and $1B in Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing. Smaller industry pockets include Engineering Services at $179M and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Propulsion Unit and Propulsion Unit Parts Manufacturing at $123M."
      }
    ]
  },
